#+TITLE:                       *cfMesh README*
#+AUTHOR:                      Franjo Juretic.
#+DATE:                           October 2016
#+LINK:                  http://www.cfmesh.com
#+OPTIONS:

cfMesh is a library for mesh generation built on OpenFOAM.

* This repository
  cfMesh for the OpenFOAM of the OpenFOAM Foundation (OpenFOAM-14), maintained
  by LEC GmbH. It starts from https://gitlab.com/openfoam/community/cfmesh and
  differs from it as follows:

  + Parallelisation is shared-memory (OpenMP) only; the MPI layer is removed.
  + One executable, cfMesh, runs all generators. The generator is selected
    with -mode or meshMode in meshDict (cartesian, cartesian2D, tet,
    polyhedral); the scripts in bin (cartesianMesh, cartesian2DMesh, tetMesh,
    pMesh) call it.
  + The stages follow snappyHexMesh: castellatedMesh, snap and addLayers are
    switches in meshDict, and the mesh is written after each stage. -region,
    -mesh, -dict, -overwrite and -noOverwrite are supported.
  + insidePoints selects which disconnected regions of the surface are meshed.
  + The objectRefinement type surface refines the cells inside a closed
    surface.
  + distLevels and distCellSizes in localRefinement give several refinement
    shells around one patch.
  + Settings that had a keyword and a dictionary form in meshDict are
    dictionaries only.
  + cfMesh's own containers are replaced by OpenFOAM's, and utilities that
    duplicate OpenFOAM tools are removed.

  To build, set the OpenFOAM-14 environment and run ./Allwmake. The library
  and the utilities install to $FOAM_SITE_LIBBIN and $FOAM_SITE_APPBIN; add
  bin to PATH for the scripts. The sections below are those of the original
  cfMesh.

  The work of LEC GmbH in this repository was done with the support of an
  AI coding assistant (Claude Code by Anthropic). AGENTS.md holds the
  guidance for such assistants.

